- `len(gr.Hits) > 0`: log hits (below), set `GuardRule`/`GuardField` from `gr.Hits[0]`, `record(OutcomeScanFailed)`, return as above.\n74:     - `gr.OptionalErr != nil`: log `scanner.guard_failed`, set `GuardRule = \"scan-error\"`. If `cfg.Redact.Gitleaks.BlockAutocloseWhenMissing` or `!role.Autoclose`: `record(OutcomeScanFailed)` and return; nothing changes. Otherwise run **close-only autoclose** (below), then `record(OutcomeError)` if `ex.errs` is non-empty, else `record(OutcomeScanFailed)`, and return. No new run outcome.\n75-     - Clean: the run continues exactly as today.\n76:   - **Close-only autoclose.** `plan := Diff(snap, sr.Findings, true, start)`; build `ex` as today with a new field `closeOnly: true`; call only `ex.edits(plan, views)`. Skip grouping, joins, creates and `touchSeen`. In `edits`, when `e.closeOnly`, do not collect `plan.Resurface` or re-rates (`plan.Seen` severity changes). In `editIssue`, when `e.closeOnly`, return before any write unless `allChecked(lines)` after the gone ticks: an issue is only ticked when it is about to be closed, so nothing is partly edited. Hold and running-job deferrals are unchanged. The writes are then: tick gone lines on that issue's existing body, the \"No longer detected\" comment, the close, and the gone/fixed rows of findings this run did not report. None of them carries text from this run's findings.\n77-   - **Logging (A6 as amended by owner answer 2).** Hits: one `log.Warn(\"scanner.guard_flagged\", \"finding\", h.Index, \"field\", h.Field, \"rule\", h.Rule)` per hit, at most 20, then `log.Warn(\"scanner.guard_flagged_total\", \"hits\", len(gr.Hits))`. Never the title, fingerprint, value or any field text. Pass failures: `log.Warn(\"scanner.guard_failed\", \"rule\", \"scan-error\", \"pass\", \"builtin\"|\"gitleaks\", \"reason\", \"timeout\"|\"error\", \"error\", err.Error())`, with `reason = \"timeout\"` when `errors.Is(err, context.DeadlineExceeded)`; the gitleaks case adds `\"autoclose\", \"allowed\"|\"blocked\"`. Logging `err.Error()` is allowed for pass failures only, because `redact` errors carry no scanned text by contract.\n78-   - **Route labels.** `create`: labels `labels.Scanner(name)` plus the route label when non-empty. `fetch` synthetic branch: the same list, so dry-run joins match. `execution` carries the route label (computed once in `Run`).\n79-   - **Join semantics (A9).** `joinableIssue(lbls []string, scanner, routeLbl string, p Parsed, group string) bool`: open-issue checks unchanged (`HasSpan`, group); the issue's `ard:` labels, compared case-insensitively, must be exactly `{labels.Scanner(scanner)}` plus `routeLbl` when non-empty. Any other `ard:` label (including `ard:pending` under `none` or `needs-human`, `ard:hold`, any `:running`) makes it not joinable, so an issue a human promoted to triage is never appended to. Update both callers (`joinable`, `join`). `openIssues` stays keyed on the scanner label, so `max_open` counts every route.\n80-\n81-6. **Stale closer (owner answer 1).** No code change: `stale.go`'s query and `decide.go`'s `precheck` require `ard:pending` and exclude `ard:needs-human`, so `none` and `needs-human` issues are never stale-closed. Lock this in with tests (Test plan). Widening is #204's job.\n82-\n--\n88-   - Step 5 (group): \"not yet claimed\" means no `ard:` label besides `ard:scanner:<name>` and the route's label. Step 6 (file): created with `ard:scanner:<name>` plus the route's label.\n89-   - Stale-closer paragraph: `route: none` and `needs-human` issues lack `ard:pending` and are never candidates (#204 may widen this).\n90:   - \"Optional gitleaks pass (#89)\" paragraph (~line 156): add `redact.gitleaks.block_autoclose_when_missing` (default false) and that the scanner guard also runs the pass.\n91-   - Configuration (~line 422): add `route` to the per-role key list.\n92-   - No credential-shaped literal anywhere in the proposal.\n93-\n94-### Test plan\n95-\n96-Command: `go test ./internal/config/... ./internal/scanner/... ./internal/roles/...`, then `make lint test` (with `GOCACHE` set to a writable dir). Build every secret-shaped string at run time from pieces (`\"AK\" + \"IA\" + ...`), as `internal/redact`'s tests do; never a credential-shaped literal (the worker diff guard holds literals).\n--\n98-- **Config (`load_test.go`, `render_test.go`).**\n99-  - `TestRoute` table: each of the three values loads on an executable scanner; defaults (executable scanner `pending`, LLM scanner `none`); `route: sometimes` errors on the `.route` key; `route: pending` on an LLM scanner errors with the \"LLM scanners may not use pending\" message; `route: none` on a triage, worker and reviewer role errors with `only valid for scanners roles`.\n100:  - Extend `TestLoadRedactGitleaks`: absent gives `BlockAutocloseWhenMissing: false`; `{enabled: true, block_autoclose_when_missing: true}` gives true; `{block_autoclose_when_missing: false}` gives false. Extend the error table: `block_autoclose_when_missing: [1]` errors on `redact.gitleaks.block_autoclose_when_missing`; the unknown-key case still errors.\n101-  - Golden: `resolved.golden` shows `block_autoclose_when_missing: false` and the scanners' `route:`.\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FzmyhChAL3wzuyj1NznejK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
